# PLAN CLI LSP — 12 agents for product completion

File: openOODA/audit/plan_cli_lsp.oot
Ship 1. Product path is cli/lsp_*.oo. vscode launches `bin/ooda lsp`.
Today initialize advertises hover, documentSymbol, definition. Not completion.
ooda/lsp/ has a catalog. It is not wired. Do not make that folder the server.

## 0. Done when

  1. initialize JSON includes completionProvider.
     Trigger characters include `&`.
  2. A buffer with `&Fs` at the cursor returns an item labeled `&FsCap`.
  3. Prefix uses line/character + lsp_ident_at. Not a fake `"prefix"` key.
     VS Code does not send `"prefix"`. ooda/lsp/ is wrong on that point.
  4. Empty prefix still returns the catalog (not a hang, not a crash).
  5. Hover and definition still name the identifier under the cursor.
     Lock: scripts/lsp_cursor_smoke.oo still prints PASSED.
  6. New lock: scripts/lsp_complete_smoke.oo prints PASSED.
  7. A test that greps the catalog in source is not enough.

## 1. Waves

  Wave 0 (read): COORD, RT, DOCS
  Wave 1 (write): DE1, DE2, HARN  — disjoint files
  Wave 2 (lock): HYG
  Wave 3 (attack): PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM
  Wave 4 (prove): INT
  Wave 5 (merge note): COORD

## 2. Twelve agents

  COORD
    Own the worktree. Name the branch `wip/lsp-complete`.
    Assign files. Refuse any edit outside the ship 1 write set.
    After INT: write audit/plan1_coord.oot with pass/fail per claim.

  DE1
    Own cli/lsp_reply.oo.
    Advertise completionProvider on initialize.
    Dispatch textDocument/completion to DE2's helper.
    If the file would pass 256 lines, split dispatch only. Do not
    rewrite hover or definition.
    Keep shutdown and unknown methods as they are.

  DE2
    Own new cli/lsp_complete.oo.
    Lift the catalog (caps, keywords, types, builtins) from
    ooda/lsp/lsp_completion.oo into the CLI folder.
    Filter by prefix from lsp_ident_at (include a leading `&`).
    Return LSP CompletionList JSON.
    Do not import ooda/lsp/. Same-folder imports only.

  RT
    Read only. Prove no chs_rt change is required.
    If emit of new CLI files fails, name the exact error.
    Do not patch runtime. Do not patch oodac.
    Write audit/plan1_rt.oot.

  HARN
    Own fixtures/lsp_complete_probe.oo and scripts/lsp_complete_smoke.oo.
    Drive the rebuilt bin/ooda lsp with framed JSON-RPC:
      initialize, then textDocument/completion on a file URI.
    Assert `&FsCap` is in the result. Assert isIncomplete is false.
    Hang budget 10 seconds.

  PV1
    Attack: completion on a missing file URI, a directory URI,
    and a body with no position. Must not crash. Must not hang.
    Must not read a path with `..`.

  PV2
    Attack: the old lsp_cursor_smoke must still pass.
    Completion must not change the hover string for `add` vs `main`.
    If a builder "fixed" hover to first-fn-only, fail the ship.

  SEC
    Completion reads a file:// path. Refuse `..`, absolute paths
    outside the worktree if the current hover loader is loose.
    Do not introduce process_exec. Do not print file bodies to logs.

  MEM
    Catalog build must not loop. Empty file, 0-byte file, huge
    prefix: bound the item list (HARN names the cap, default 64).
    No new long-lived buffers.

  INT
    Rebuild CLI with seed oodac. Run lsp_cursor_smoke and
    lsp_complete_smoke twice in a clean shell (double-run).
    Confirm strings on bin/ooda still say `pure .oo product CLI`.
    Confirm oodac/oodac was not overwritten.

  HYG
    Line counts. Academy headers. No `.md` / `.py`. No tmp.c left
    in the worktree. dinner_lint on the ship files.

  DOCS
    Do not edit the public site. Do not edit ROADMAP as truth.
    One audit note: what initialize advertises now vs before.
    If SHIPPED is later updated, it waits on skeptic pass.

## 3. Failure

  First irrecoverable fail stops the ship. COORD writes why.
  Do not start ship-merge. Other ships may continue.
